an enforce that contract. The fund's own obligations to service providers don't disappear, though. Those providers can look to the series' assets, which are ring-fenced from other series under the trust's series provisions, and the trustees may need to waive fees, suspend operations, or liquidate the series if assets are insufficient.\n\n**Caveat:** Specifics depend on the trust agreement, the expense agreement, and the sponsor's contract terms, so check those documents for the actual allocation of liability. This is general industry context, not legal advice.","ttft_ms":3935,"type":"result","duration_ms":5456,"uuid":"606a51d9-3917-426d-98fd-30fd3329de69","ttft_stream_ms":489,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":489,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
